Opaque focus (dcsvr_two_layers_alpha=3 with dcsvr_two_layers; native/quadviews/dcsvr_twolayer_ps.hlsl): the runtime is
never asked to alpha-blend. The focus layer goes out with no blend flags (neither BLEND_TEXTURE_SOURCE_ALPHA nor
UNPREMULTIPLIED_ALPHA) over its whole rectangle, with its normal field of view, and its output pass writes the composed
result there itself: the focus colour as with 0 (edge match tent, Far depth, fill) blended over the periphery image
(t3, the source the periphery layer shows) with the composition's fade, alpha 1. The periphery is read where the
composition reads it for the same direction: the (moved) focus uv times the focus view's span plus its offset in the
periphery's uv (dcsvrBand, from both fields of view; the constants grow to 128 bytes). Where the fade is 1 the colour is
the focus colour exactly, so the sharp area is the same as with 0; outside the shape (the corners of a round focus) the
layer shows the periphery. The periphery layer is as with 0. debug_focus_view: the periphery black, as the composition.
Read at start only, one log line; 0, 1 and 2 are as before, byte for byte (tests/quadviews-composition).
